      "diagnosis": "The phone number is hardcoded to '0000000000' in the data.customer object within updateConfirmFrame, causing the submitted phone to lose the user's input.",
      "evidence_explained": "\"saved\":{\"appointments\":[{\"start\":\"2026-11-02 09:00:00\",\"end\":\"2026-11-02 09:30:00\"}],\"customers\":[{\"first_name\":\"Synthetic\",\"last_name\":\"PhonePersistence\",\"email\":\"phone-persistence@example.invalid\",\"phone_number\":\"0000000000\"}]},\"expected\":{\"start\":\"2026-11-02 09:00:00\",\"customer\":{\"first_name\":\"Synthetic\",\"last_name\":\"PhonePersistence\",\"email\":\"phone-persistence@example.invalid\",\"phone_number\":\"0000000042\"}}",
      "reasoning": "We need to understand why phone number gets overwritten with zeros. In the evidence, saved phone_number is \"0000000000\" instead of \"0000000042\". Looking at booking.js line 823: inside updateConfirmFrame, data.customer.phone_number is set to '0000000000'. That seems to be the bug: they hardcode phone number to zeros instead of taking from $phoneNumber.val(). Indeed line 823 shows: phone_number: '0000000000', Should be $phoneNumber.val(). Let's check context: around line 823 in the provided file snippet.\n\nWe saw snippet:\n\n        data.customer = {\n            last_name: $lastName.val(),\n            first_name: $firstName.val(),\n            email: $email.val(),\n            phone_number: '0000000000',\n            address: $address.val(),\n            city: $city.val(),\n            zip_code: $zipCode.val(),\n            timezone: $selectTimezone.val(),\n            custom_field_1: $customField1.val(),\n            custom_field_2: $customField2.val(),\n            custom_field_3: $customField3.val(),\n            custom_field_4: $customField4.val(),\n            custom_field_5: $customField5.val(),\n        };\n\nThus the bug is there. Need to replace that line with phone_number: $phoneNumber.val(),\n\nAlso need to ensure that when reopening (manageMode) the phone number is correctly loaded from customer data. In applyAppointmentData, line $phoneNumber.val(customer.phone_number); looks fine.\n\nThus fix: edit assets/js/pages/booking.js line.\n\nLet's also verify that there aren't other places where phone number is forced. Search for '0000000000' maybe only there.\n\nNow propose edit.\n\nWe need to provide evidence_explained quoting the verifier evidence: saved phone_number \"0000000000\" vs expected \"0000000042\". So we quote that.\n\nNow produce propose_repair.",
